## Layer boundaries

- `api/` — HTTP only: routing, request/response schemas, status codes. No PyTorch or file I/O.
- `application/` — use cases orchestrating domain ports; no framework imports.
- `domain/` — entities, exceptions, port interfaces; no FastAPI, PyTorch, or OpenCV.
- `infrastructure/` — adapters implementing ports (YOLO engine, image processors, `local_model_repository` for `models/`).
- `app/` — FastAPI app factory, lifespan (load model on startup from `models/`), DI wiring.

## Inference and API behavior

- `POST /api/v1/inference` — multipart image upload; return detections with bounding boxes, confidence, and request id.
- `GET /api/v1/health` — liveness; include model loaded flag when readiness is required.
- `GET /api/v1/model` — metadata from loaded weights (version, classes, input size) without exposing filesystem paths.
- Validate MIME type, size limits, and dimensions before inference.
- Map domain exceptions to consistent error schemas in `api/v1/schemas/errors.py`.

## Configuration

- `configs/model.yaml` — `weights_path` (relative to project root, under `models/`), confidence threshold, device, warmup settings.
- `configs/app.yaml` — host, port, max upload size, CORS.
- Secrets and overrides via environment variables; provide `.env.example`.

## Quality bar

- Type-annotate public APIs; run mypy on `src/`.
- Unit tests for validation, mapping, and metadata; integration tests for health and inference with httpx.
- Structured JSON logs; never log raw image bytes or secrets.
- Docker image must copy or mount `models/` and run warmup in lifespan or `scripts/warmup_model.py`.
